# Course documents: copyrighted, kept locally only (D-034). Partners use their own copies.
/project.pdf
/DoronDubnov_revised.pdf
/nlp-intro-short.pptx

# Manual-audit sheets quote full corpus sentences: local only, never in the public repo (D-042).
# Regenerate with `uv run hebloc pilot audit`; Ori's filled copies are backed up under data/backups/.
/annotation/pilot_audit.csv
/annotation/pilot_audit_words.csv

# Regenerable review that quotes raw corpus text (uv run hebloc prepare --sample N)
/docs/m2_sample_review.md

# Secrets and local tool settings: never commit
.env
*.env
*.pem
*.key
.claude/settings.local.json

# Interrupted `hebloc corpora install` staging (removed automatically on the next run)
/.corpora-staging/

# SILVER annotation (D-061; annotation/S56_SILVER_PROTOCOL.md §8). Private: everything that quotes corpus text or
# holds labels (job inputs, workspaces, transcripts, pass files, final silver files) lives under /data/ or OUTSIDE the
# repo (~/hebloc-silver-ws). In git only: the protocol, the prompts, the worked examples (texts already in the
# guideline), the anchor ids (no frames) and FROZEN_SILVER.json (ids + hashes).
/annotation/silver/*
!/annotation/silver/prompts/
!/annotation/silver/worked_examples.csv
!/annotation/silver/anchor_ids.csv
!/annotation/silver/FROZEN_SILVER.json
*_silver.csv
silver-ws/
hebloc-silver-ws/
*.jsonl
QC_STOP.md
# The paper-example frame key stays out of git until the anchor silver is delivered (D-061, a physical guard).
/annotation/gold/mikra_paper_examples.csv
# Withdrawn / unsent drafts (the A7 draft for Efrat was withdrawn by D-061)
/docs/drafts/
